Try adding the friend mechanism to allow method call cross side-by-side modules.

For the `hello.rs` example, now we can pass a `reg.write` method as a friend into the `A2B_i4` module.

In cmtrs, 

```rust
fn add1(reg: &Reg, t: &Type) -> A2B {
  let io = io! { T: t};
  friend!(reg); // here declare the reg as a friend
  let pass = method!((io.a) -> (io.b) {
      reg.write(&io.a); // here invoke reg.write
      ret!(io.a + 1.lit(t))
    }
  );
  //...
}
#[module]
fn add_top() -> A2B {
  let t = Type::UInt(4);
  let io = io! {T : &t};
  distinguisher!("top");
  let reg = instance!(stl::reg(&t));
  let add1_impl = instance!(add1(&reg, &t)); // here, pass the reg inside add1 generator
  //...
}
```

In cmtir,

```lisp
(module "A2B_i4" (
  (annotations {"synthesis":true,"cmtrs_span":"..."})
  (inputs (%a:i4))
  (outputs (%b:i4 %reg.in:i4))
  (wires ())
  (native
    (instances) (friends ; here declare friend methods
      ("reg.write" method (%reg.in:i4) () (single_cycle) true "reg.write_enable" "reg.write_ready")
    ))
  (rules ...)))
(module "A2B_i4_top" (
  (annotations {"cmtrs_span":"...","is_top":true,"synthesis":true})
  (inputs (%a:i4))
  (outputs (%b:i4))
  (wires ())
  (native
    (instances
      ("reg" "Reg_i4" (friends))
      ("add1_impl" "A2B_i4" (friends
        reg.write ; here pass the friend param
      ))
    ) (friends))
    (rules ...)))
```



Below are Cursor-summarized diffs:

1. Rule Signature Changes:
```rust:crates/cmtc/examples/counter_generated.rs
// ... existing code ...
cmtir::RuleSignature {
  ty: cmtir::RuleTy::Method,
  inputs: vec![io.a.value_id().unwrap()],
  outputs: vec![io.b.value_id().unwrap()], 
  side_effect: Some(true),
  timing: cmtir::RuleTiming::SingleCycle,
  enable: None,
  ready: None,
}
// ... existing code ...
```

The rule signature has been refactored to use a single struct with a `ty` field rather than separate enum variants. This consolidates the signature fields into one structure.

2. Friend Functionality:
```rust:crates/cmtrs/src/interface.rs
// ... existing code ...
fn friend<T: Instance>(ctx: &ContextItfc<Self>, friend: &T) -> T {
  let mut binding = ctx.borrow_mut();
  let module = binding.as_mut().unwrap().module_mut();
  let friend_path = friend.path();
  let mut friend_rule_mapping = IndexMap::new();
  // ... friend implementation ...
}
// ... existing code ...
```

Added new friend functionality that allows modules to share methods and state. This includes:
- Friend method mapping
- Value mapping between friends
- Friend prefix registration
- Friend rule signatures

3. Instance Trait Changes:
```rust:crates/cmtrs/src/interface.rs
pub trait Instance: ToIOMacro<Output = Self> + Sized + 'static {
  // ... existing code ...
  fn path(&self) -> Vec<String>;
  fn as_friend<T: Itfc>(&self, mapping: IndexMap<String, String>, ctx: &Rc<RefCell<Option<T>>>) -> Self;
  fn friend_params(&self) -> Vec<ir::PathRule>;
  // ... existing code ...
}
```

The Instance trait has been extended to support friend functionality with new required methods.

4. Module Macro Changes:
```rust:crates/cmtrs_macros/src/lib.rs
#[proc_macro_attribute]
pub fn module(attr: TokenStream, macro_input: TokenStream) -> TokenStream {
  let directives = parse_macro_input!(attr as Directives);
  // ... module implementation with directives ...
}
```

The module macro now supports directives for configuration, including synthesis and friend-related options.

These changes appear to be focused on:
1. Simplifying and consolidating rule signatures
2. Adding friend functionality for module composition
3. Extending the Instance trait to support friends
4. Improving module configuration through directives


Issues to be resolved:

- [x] Conflict resolving. Currently, I straightly use the "ready" signal of the be-friend method, which doesn't always exist, for example, in the ext-module Reg. The better solution should be friend-aware global conflict resolution.
- [x] Dangling friend. `cmtrs` currently only supports using one instance to declare friends in another instance. It cannot declare friends in the top module.
